# Authentication and User Management Patterns

## User Registration Implementation

### 1. Registration Flow Best Practices

- Create password credential **before** creating user record to fail fast
- Use proper validation through the password hasher (don't implement custom validation)
- Implement proper cleanup on failures
- Auto-login users after successful registration

### 2. Registration Action Pattern

```typescript
export const RegisterAction: RequestAction<RegisterActionType> = async ({ injector, getBody }) => {
  const logger = getLogger(injector).withScope('Register')
  const { username, password } = await getBody()

  const storeManager = injector.getInstance(StoreManager)
  const authenticator = injector.getInstance(PasswordAuthenticator)

  // Check if user exists first
  const userStore = storeManager.getStoreFor(User, 'username')
  const existingUser = await userStore.get(username)
  if (existingUser) {
    await logger.warning({ message: `Registration attempt for existing user: ${username}` })
    throw new RequestError('User already exists', 409)
  }

  try {
    // Create credential first (fail fast if invalid)
    const credential = await authenticator.hasher.createCredential(username, password)

    // Create user
    const newUser: User = {
      username,
      roles: [], // Default to empty roles for new users
      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),
      updatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
    }

    await userStore.add(newUser)
    await storeManager.getStoreFor(PasswordCredential, 'userName').add(credential)

    return JsonResult({ username: newUser.username, roles: newUser.roles })
  } catch (error) {
    // Cleanup on failure
    try {
      await userStore.remove(username)
    } catch (cleanupError) {
      // Log but don't fail on cleanup errors
    }
    throw new RequestError('Registration failed', 400)
  }
}
```

### 3. Frontend Integration

- Add registration method to SessionService
- Follow the same pattern as login method
- Show appropriate success/error notifications
- Navigate to appropriate route after successful registration

### 4. Session Service Pattern

```typescript
public async register(username: string, password: string): Promise<void> {
  await usingAsync(this.operation(), async () => {
    try {
      const { result: usr } = await this.api.call({
        method: 'POST',
        action: '/register',
        body: { username, password }
      })

      // Auto-login after registration
      this.currentUser.setValue({ username: usr.username, roles: usr.roles })
      this.state.setValue('authenticated')

      this.notys.emit('onNotyAdded', {
        body: 'Welcome to PI-RAT!',
        title: 'Account created successfully',
        type: 'success',
      })
    } catch (error) {
      this.loginError.setValue(error instanceof Error ? error.message : '')
      this.notys.emit('onNotyAdded', {
        body: 'Please check your details and try again',
        title: 'Registration failed',
        type: 'warning',
      })
    }
  })
}
```

## Error Handling Patterns

### 1. HTTP Status Codes

- `409 Conflict` - User already exists
- `400 Bad Request` - Invalid input/validation errors
- `401 Unauthorized` - Authentication required
- `403 Forbidden` - Insufficient permissions

### 2. User-Friendly Messages

- Don't expose internal errors to users
- Provide clear, actionable error messages
- Log detailed errors server-side for debugging
- Use consistent error message patterns

## Security Best Practices

### 1. Password Handling

- Never log passwords or credentials
- Let the framework handle password validation
- Use secure credential creation methods
- Don't implement custom password validation

### 2. User Creation

- Default to minimal permissions (empty roles)
- Validate user input appropriately
- Use proper logging for security events
- Implement proper session management

### 3. Form Validation

- Validate on both client and server side
- Use consistent validation patterns
- Provide real-time feedback when appropriate
- Handle edge cases gracefully

## UI/UX Patterns

### 1. Registration Forms

- Include confirm password field
- Provide clear validation feedback
- Disable form during submission
- Show loading states appropriately

### 2. Navigation Flow

- Easy access to registration from login
- Clear navigation back to login
- Proper route handling for authenticated users
- Consistent navigation patterns

### 3. Success/Error States

- Clear success messages after registration
- Helpful error messages with next steps
- Consistent notification styling
- Proper form state management
